From: procyonid <312394225+procyonid@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Bind zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 at version 1 too.

The server-side decoration support only bound zxdg_decoration_manager_v1
when the compositor offered version 2, so compositors that offer version 1,
like niri and other Smithay-based compositors, always got Wine's own title
bar and frame. Version 2 only adds the invalid_mode protocol error; the
requests, events and modes are the same, and Wine only sends valid modes.
Bind at the offered version, up to 2.

Fix by procyonid (https://github.com/procyonid), tested on niri 26.04.
Packaged as a GE-Proton patch by GloriousEggroll.

Fixes: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/955
---
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c
@@ -534,9 +534,9 @@
     else if (strcmp(interface, "zxdg_decoration_manager_v1") == 0)
     {
         if (wayland_disable_ssd()) return;
-        if (version < 2) return;
         process_wayland.zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 =
-            wl_registry_bind(registry, id, &zxdg_decoration_manager_v1_interface, 2);
+            wl_registry_bind(registry, id, &zxdg_decoration_manager_v1_interface,
+                             version < 2 ? version : 2);
     }
     else if (strcmp(interface, "wp_color_manager_v1") == 0)
     {
